    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Emigrant began as a railroad stop that served the area's mining and agricultural activities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emigrant%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town's name comes from nearby Emigrant Peak, which rises to 10,960 feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/emigrant_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gold was first discovered in Emigrant Gulch in 1863 by Thomas Curry, sparking a rush of miners.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/emigrant_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1866, the nearby mining camp Yellowstone City was abandoned as gold ran out and hostilities rose.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/emigrant_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community sits between the Absaroka and Gallatin Ranges in Paradise Valley, overlooking the Yellowstone River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emigrant%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Emigrant's elevation is about 4,875 feet, placing it in a high‑altitude continental climate with hot summers and cold winters.",
